        "t_min": "°C",
        "precipitation": "mm",
        "radiation": "MJ/m²"
      }
    },
    "weatherLocations": {
      "NT": {
        "label": "Humpty Doo (Darwin rural area), NT",
        "latitude": -12.6,
        "longitude": 131.25
      },
      "QLD": {
        "label": "Mareeba, QLD",
        "latitude": -16.99,
        "longitude": 145.42
      }
    },
    "changes": "MangoDMC_NIR_Data_v3.csv, fruit temperature No/Mid only; replicate scans averaged per fruit; seasons 1-3 (Cal+Tuning) = train, season 4 (Val Ext) = test, as the authors define; up to 12 train / 15 test fruits per harvest event (seed 20261121); 245 bands 405-1137 nm (zero padding outside the detector range dropped). Weather: daily max/min temperature (°C), precipitation (mm) and shortwave radiation (MJ/m²) over the 90 days up to the harvest date, at one representative location per region.",
    "limitation": "The source gives only the region (NT or QLD) and the date (taken as the harvest date), not orchard coordinates: weather comes from one representative location per region, is shared by every fruit of a harvest, and day 0 is the full local day of that date. Harvests of one region and season share most of their weather window, so folds are grouped by region x season and season 4 is the held-out test. Results use this subset and protocol and are not comparable with the publications' own splits."
  }
